WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.840
Declassified U.S. government documents and witness testimony from former or

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:13.000
retired U.S. military personnel confirm beyond any doubt the reality of ongoing

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.100
UFO incursions at nuclear weapons sites. When I say UFO, the witnesses have

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:30.000
described these craft as disc-shaped or cylindrical shape or spherical. These objects are capable

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.590
of both hovering and high-velocity flight, usually completely silently.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:45.300
Over the past 37 years, I have personally located and interviewed more than 120 of these

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:51.640
former or retired military personnel, all of whom report UFO incidents at one or more

00:00:51.640 --> 00:01:00.000
of the following locations: nuclear missile sites, nuclear weapons storage areas, and

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
sites in Nevada and the Pacific during the era of atomic atmospheric testing.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.720
Sometime in the evening hours on March 24th, I received a call from one of my top site

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.780
guards, the flight security controller, stating that they had been observing strange lights

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:24.030
in the sky, making odd maneuvers, and wanted to report it. I thought it was kind of a strange

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:30.000
report, but I took it seriously. You have to understand, we were protecting nuclear

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.450
weapons and the reports we generally got were very professional.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.970
At any rate, I kind of dismissed the call.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.610
He called back about five minutes later.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:49.770
This time he was screaming into the phone saying they're looking at an object, a red

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.690
glowing object hovering just above our front gate.

00:01:53.690 --> 00:02:00.000
Right above us, there's a huge white thing pulsating light above us.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.330
And I had to call them to make sure I wasn't seeing anything.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:09.410
Upon prodding, he told us it was shaped like a fat cigar.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.650
I think he said a pregnant cigar.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.230
White pulsating light between the pulsations,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:18.130
he saw red and blue lights.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:20.970
It was silent because I prodded him saying,

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.970
is it some form a helicopter?

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.560
He said, no, it's very silent.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.580
We're talking to him for several minutes.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.000
And he says, it's starting to move away along

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.510
access route. I believe, these gentlemen believe, that this planet is being visited

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:42.330
by beings from another world who, for whatever reason, have taken an interest in the nuclear

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:50.230
arms race which began at the end of World War II. Regarding the missile shutdown incidents,

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:56.280
my opinion, their opinion, is that whoever are aboard these craft are sending a signal

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.000
to both Washington and Moscow, among others, that we are

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.910
playing with fire. That the possession and threatened use of nuclear weapons potentially

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:12.010
threatens the human race and the integrity of the planetary environment.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:16.040
If you should see one out in the field. And he proceeded to tell me what to do. If we're

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:21.700
out on the road, we see a UFO. We do not go to the launcher, but instead to the nearest

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.260
launch control facility. Also, we call job control and let them know what we're doing.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.000
If we're at a site and we're penetrating, then we have to stop

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.050
what we're doing, remove ourselves from the site, call job control. We all have radio

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:40.270
controls, radio contact with all these. It's called a job control and wait for further

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:44.260
instructions. Now, if we're at the site and we're doing our work, I'm going to have to

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:49.420
take myself, my team, and the targeting tapes, go into the launcher, close the personnel

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:55.030
hatch. Now, all the teams, before you go out into the field, will take with us an armed

00:03:55.030 --> 00:04:00.000
guard. That's just normal. We have to leave the one guard, armed

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.990
guard on top all by himself and he's supposed to report to job control or the launch control

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:11.440
facility or what he was seeing and he said and i says okay but then he says one other

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.240
thing don't leave yet we're going to hold everybody back until we're sure that all the

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.970
activity out in the field has ceased at least for the time being so i waited around about

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:25.700
an hour and a half we was all ready to go and they contacted me and says okay you can

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:30.000
go now so i went with my team we went out to the field

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:35.320
We restarted. We had to go to Oscar Flight. That's not a very pleasant thing.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.820
Oscar Flight is 120 miles. It's the furthest flight from the base.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.180
And in Air Force trucks, that's not the most comfortable ride.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:47.940
But nevertheless, we went out to Oscar Flight and restarted, I think it was either three or four missiles.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.350
This is where Bob was at the time.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.850
We restarted three or four of their missiles.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.100
The startups were successful, and I saw no incidents in the field.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.250
WHEN I CAME BACK,

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.070
we have to go through debriefing first things I asked him upon return to the

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:03.670
base

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:08.210
what about this missile out in belt he said as soon as daylight came he was

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.100
going to send choppers over

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:15.360
it was nighttime when he first saw it and he wasn't going to have him scale

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.080
down the

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.580
mountain at nighttime so they were going to send some choppers down and scale the

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.300
mountain

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.780
scale the canyon daylight time but as soon as daylight time came up this thing shot

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:24.990
up right through the

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:30.000
everything just disappeared more or less so that

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:40.100
was that. Now, also, about a week later, I also heard that a UFO was sighted over

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.550
India flight, and there was a partial shutdown. I think four or five missiles

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:48.780
shut down at India flight with a UFO overhead, not the whole flight, and I had

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:53.630
to go out and restart at least two of them. And then the rest of my time at

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:57.250
Montana, I was involved in no more further UFO incidents, nothing else

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.000
happened. And then I...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:15.250
went on elsewhere. Thank you. Good afternoon. My name is Charles I. Halt. I retired from

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:21.350
the U.S. Air Force in 1991 as a colonel. During my military career, I was base commander of

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:26.570
two large installations, and at the time of my retirement, I was in the Department of

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:30.000
Defense Inspector General's office with total inspection oversight of all

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:35.490
services and all service agencies. In 1980 I was reassigned from the Pentagon

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:40.740
to RAF Bentwaters as a deputy base commander. At that time Bentwaters was

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.240
one of the largest tactical fighter rings in the world. We had the two base

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.800
complex Woodbridge and Bentwaters in England and four FOLs in Germany and two

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:55.180
additional standby bases. In December 1980, early in the morning, several of our

00:06:55.180 --> 00:07:00.000
security policemen discovered strange lights in the forest in East Anglia just out

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.160
outside the back gate of RAF Woodbridge. Three patrolmen, Sergeant Penniston, Airman Burroughs,

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:11.900
and Airman Cabanasak actually were dispatched into the forest and approached a craft. They

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:19.200
reported it being triangular, approximately three meters on a side, dark metallic in appearance

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:24.730
with strange markings. They were observed it for a period of time and it very quickly

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:30.000
and silently vanished at high speed. Initially, I was not a

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.280
aware of all the details, I was only told of strange lights,

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:36.680
and I was sure there was a logical explanation.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.750
Two nights later, at the family Christmas party,

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:40.980
we were interrupted.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.260
The on-duty flight commander for the security police

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.280
squadron, Lieutenant Bruce England,

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.380
came and approached the base commander and I.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.290
He was white as a sheet.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.900
He said, it's back.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.020
He said, what's back?

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.950
He said, the UFO.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.780
Well, we still were, I should say,

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.930
non-believers at that point.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.000
Since my boss had to do the presentations,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.740
I was tasked, unfortunately, to investigate.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.960
So I went home and changed clothes.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.700
I didn't really expect it to find a logical explanation.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.140
I took several security policemen with me,

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.660
a disaster preparedness NCO who took an APN 27,

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.000
a Gagger Conner, and a camera.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.020
I also had my small cassette recorder

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.390
I carried everywhere when I was on duty.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.670
I was taken to the supposed site.

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:29.410
We find indentations approximately an inch and a half deep

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.750
approximately six to eight feet on a side and radiation of eight to nine times normal background radiation

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.470
Not enough to be dangerous to somebody but significant

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:46.840
We also find broken branches on the trees while we were milling around trying to make sense of the whole thing

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:54.000
One of the individuals with me suddenly spotted something off through the forest with a bright glowing object

00:08:54.120 --> 00:09:00.000
The best way I can describe that it looked like an eye was bright red with a dark center

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:03.190
It appeared to be winking, it would sort of wink.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:07.050
It was shedding something like molten metal was dripping off it.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:10.330
It silently moved through the trees, avoiding any contact.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.340
It bobbed up and down, and at one point it actually approached us.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.050
We tried to get closer.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:19.340
It receded out into the field, beyond the forest,

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:23.990
and silently exploded into five white objects, gone.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:26.290
So we went out into the field looking for any evidence

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.000
because something had apparently been falling off it, and we found nothing.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.920
But while we were searching around in the field,

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.560
one of the people with me noticed some objects in the sky to the north.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.450
There were three or four objects in the north, brightly colored,

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.140
changing from elliptical to round,

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:45.770
and moving at very high speed and sharp angular movements

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.230
as though they were doing a grid search.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.250
While we were watching them, somebody else noticed to the south

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.800
there were two objects just sort of hovering in the sky.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:10:00.000
One object approached us at very high speed, best guess is 3 to 5,000.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.440
miles and feet somewhere in that neighborhood, stopped directly overhead and sent down a

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:09.520
concentrated beam in our feet. It was about one foot in diameter. The best way I can equate

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:15.490
it is sort of a laser beam. We stood there in awe. Was this a warning? Was this an attempt

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:22.700
to communicate? Was this a weapon or just a probe? Just as suddenly as it appeared, click,

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:30.000
it disappeared. We stood there, ah, really concerned. About that time, we noticed the other

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.880
to the south was sending down beams about a mile, mile and a half away over

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:38.490
Woodbridge base. We had three different radios with us: the police radio, the

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:42.470
security police radio, and I had the command net. All three radios were

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:45.510
functional and we were talking to control centers. They were constantly

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:49.010
breaking up and we had great difficulties communicating, but we were able to

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:52.310
discern that on the police and security net that some of those

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.670
beams were either falling into or near the weapons storage area and there's a

00:10:55.670 --> 00:11:00.000
great deal of concern. It really bothered me at

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.910
the time. Every time something of significance happened that night I kind of clicked on my little

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:10.780
tape recorder and recorded it so I'd have a record of it for the next day. Unbeknownst to me a copy

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:15.920
of that was released by one of my co-workers several years later and hence it was a lot of

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:23.180
publicity. My superiors at the time were informed what happened. I briefed my boss. I played the

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:30.000
tape for him. He listened intently. He was aware of the incident because he was monitoring the night before on the radio he and several other

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.010
were. He took the tape to the Third Air Force staff meeting the following Wednesday. Third

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:38.610
Air Force was the Air Force headquarters at that time in England. Played it for General

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:45.680
Baisley, the commander and staff. They all sat silently. The decision was, it happened

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.010
off the base, so it's a British affair. In other words, they were loathe to get involved.

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:53.010
So my boss came back and threw me the tape recorder, and I said, "Well, what do we do,

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:58.080
boss?" He said, "Get with Squadron Leader Moreland, who was the British liaison officer,

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.000
and do a report. It's their problem."

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:00.740
not ours.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.100
Gosh, here I am kind of caught in the middle,

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:05.120
and I'm the junior guy here.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.360
Whoa, why did I ever get involved?

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:12.100
Well, Squadron Leader Moreland was on vacation in Wales at the time.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.680
He came back, and he was quite upset that he was in the middle of the thing, too.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.220
So he said, well, write a memo.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:20.300
So I wrote a, I shall call it, cleaned-up memo,

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.660
just kind of unexplained lights, just to kind of tickle there,

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.560
get them to come out and investigate and look into the thing.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:30.000
Well, I gave it to Moreland, unbeknownst to me, Moreland,

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.080
sent a copy to his superior third Air Force I didn't know that at the time the

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.650
copied MOD was apparently buried in the files days turned into weeks and weeks

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.950
turned into months and I almost forgot about the incident to be honest with you

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:49.970
gave up several years later one of my co-workers was playing a copy of my tape

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:54.530
cocktail parties and caught somebody's ear somebody started asking questions and

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:58.240
he said oh halt wrote a memo next thing we know there was a freedom of

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:00.000
information request came into

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.660
to Bentwaters.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.540
Of course, there was no official copy.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:04.980
We didn't have word processors in those days.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:07.240
We used typing manifolds in the old typewriters.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.360
We were just transitioning.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.440
And the only copy was an onion skin that I had in my desk.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.300
So my boss went back and said, there's no official record of it.

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:18.750
Well, somebody else found out the 3rd Air Force had a copy.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.870
Well, Pete Bent, a good personal friend of mine, was the acting 3rd Air Force commander,

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.990
called me and he said, hey, Chuck, I've got a copy of this memo.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.170
We're going to have to release it.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.510
I said, please, burn it.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.580
Your life and mine will never be the same.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:33.080
You and I don't need this.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.220
Well, need I say more?

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.600
The tape came out, unbeknownst to me.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.390
The memo came out, and a lot of publicity.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:42.250
But the events certainly happened.

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:44.270
Now, some things have happened since then.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.910
I was very innocent at the time and believed what I was told.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.830
I asked the OSI if they had an interest, and I was told, oh, no, not at all.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:52.480
Wrong.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.970
I found out later that the airmen were, how should I say, pretty harshly interrogated that were involved.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.760
I have never been debriefed.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:04.500
I also found out later that the tire operator,

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.140
that both the tire operators at Bentwaters,

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.260
saw an object and picked it up on her bright two radar

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:11.610
and watched it.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:14.070
I found out that the tire operator in a weapons storage

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.470
area actually saw something, added a comm man

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.490
who was working there, and saw it go down

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.470
into the forest near us.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:25.570
And also, several other people around the base saw it.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.880
It's kind of interesting.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.040
What did we see?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.000
I have no idea what we saw that night.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.860
I do know it was under intelligent control, and in my personal opinion, it was either

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:35.660
from another dimension or extraterrestrial.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:50.150
Good afternoon.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:53.290
My name is Jerome Nelson.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:15:00.000
From 1962 to 1965, I was an Atlas F ICBM deputy missile commander.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:10.180
crew commander assigned to the 579th Strategic Missile Squadron in Roswell, New Mexico.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:18.080
Sometime during the winter of 1963 through 1964, while I was on alert duty in the launch

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:26.790
control center at Atlas Site 9 west of Roswell, my top side security guard called me on the

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.440
telephone and reported a bright light.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:38.180
that is a fully illuminated round object was hovering silently over the missile silo and

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:44.820
shining a light down onto it. I could tell that he was serious and his voice revealed

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:51.290
he was very frightened. After perhaps five minutes, the object left the vicinity. Even

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:57.600
before it left, I called the base command post at Walker Air Force Base and reported

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.000
the incident. I was concerned.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.880
the object would somehow sabotage the missile.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:10.100
I was surprised by the response I received, being told that the command post would take

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:15.220
the unauthorized excursion under advisement.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:23.830
I was never debriefed by my commander or anyone else, which I found quite puzzling and frustrating.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:30.000
Over the next month or so, this type of incident occurred several more times while I was on

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:38.300
site 9. I would estimate the total number as more than 30 but fewer than 10. On each

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:43.280
occasion I would call the command post but each time my report was met with the

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:53.220
same apparent indifference. During each of these incidents I witnessed the guard would call the

00:16:53.220 --> 00:17:00.000
launch control center and report the UFO. Several guards were involved over time and were all

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.880
obviously frightened by the object hovering over the site their voices were

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:12.530
actually trembling because of my duties in the launch control center I could not

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:18.860
go topside and look at the objects myself only decades later that I did I

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:24.910
learned that at least one missile facility technician Bob Kaplan had been

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:30.000
ordered to report to the Office of Special Investigations on base

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:38.060
and make a report about a similar incident he had witnessed at Site-9 during the period.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:45.470
At the time this development was kept from me and my missile commander,

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:50.550
I do not know whether anyone else was interviewed by the OSI, but I wasn't.

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:53.910
That's my report.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:06.870
Well, good afternoon ladies and gentlemen. My name is Patrick McDonough and I'm here

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:14.010
today to relate an experience that happened to me in September of 1966. That's 44 years

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:20.390
ago. But that experience was so significant it was basically burned in my memory. I haven't

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:25.760
forgotten about it at all. But I am getting older and I did want to put this experience

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:30.000
and relate it on the record. A little background on

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:45.330
I had enlisted in the Air Force in Berkeley, California in the first week of November 1962 at the onset of the Cuban Missile Crisis it was going.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.250
I felt patriotic.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:51.250
And up to that time I had been studying engineering in college.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.250
I had three years of engineering.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:59.440
And the Air Force, considering my background, trained me to be a geodetic surveyor.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:06.900
I was assigned the 1381st Geodetic Survey Squadron in Orlando, Florida.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:17.720
We basically, in 1965, we moved to Warren Air Force Base in Wyoming.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:27.590
On average, I would spend nine, ten months a year on temporary duty, surveying for latitude

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:30.000
and longitude at our missile sites and aircraft.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.960
bases for positioning missile and aircraft guidance systems.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:44.690
Basically, the squadron's mission was to provide precise geographical coordinates for a missile

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:51.730
or an aircraft inertial guidance system so that the missile or aircraft would know exactly

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:58.420
precisely where it was at when it takes off, while the intelligence agencies would provide

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.000
the targeting information.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:11.200
In early September of 1966, myself and two other airmen, an Airman 1st Class Al Kramer

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:16.860
and an Airman 3rd Class Charlie Coates, we were temporarily assigned to Maelstrom Air

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:28.510
Force Base and were ordered to provide or perform the initial geodetic surveys for the

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:30.000
last 50 missile sites there.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:38.340
There already was 150 Minuteman I sites, and we were putting in the last 50 for the wing.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:45.550
And basically, we were assigned to the Site Activation Task Force they call SATAF.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:50.470
It was a Boeing, really, the prime contractor.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:21:00.000
We were given a government truck, no radio, anything in it. I was the chief of party. I was the

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:06.590
observer on our small three-man team. Al was the recorder, Charlie was, we were

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:12.240
trying to train him both in observing and recording. We arrive, normally would

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:17.950
arrive at a missile site at about an early evening. We'd set up our

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:24.010
instruments and basically what I was doing was the star observation to

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:30.000
provide precise latitude and longitude. On the night of this incident that

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.060
happened, we were completing a series of what we call celestial astroasmus

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:43.020
observations southeast of Conrad, and I was doing the observing, Al was

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:48.490
recording, and Charlie was assisting now with the chronometer on the time hacks as

00:21:48.490 --> 00:22:00.000
I tipped on Polaris. The unusual thing about this missile site I was at was that the black

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:07.090
The last hatch of the silo was open, and that was very unusual.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:10.710
Normally when I'd go to these missile sites, even though they were not activated yet with

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:13.850
a missile, they were always closed.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:14.930
The monoliths were there.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:24.290
We do four monoliths and do a precise quadriangle, and the work we did was very precise.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:30.000
that involved a lot of -- it's basically all using starship.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:38.170
And so here's the site that we arrive at and the blast hatch is open.

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:41.280
And we're nearing completion of the star observations.

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:48.670
We had been to the other three monoliths and I was at the monolith next to the hatch.

00:22:48.670 --> 00:23:00.000
And it was probably about 1:00, 1:30, and an unidentified flying object came from the north and started.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.180
It stopped right over us.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:11.870
I would say it was probably about an altitude of 300 feet or so, maybe a little higher.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:13.510
It's a little hard to tell in the dark.

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:16.210
It was round.

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:28.750
It had, I would estimate its diameter, about 50 feet, kind of like a pretty large, you know, like a wingspan of a B-52, something in that range.

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:30.000
It's pretty large.

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:34.870
It seemed to have pulsating lights going around it.

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:39.430
And it had a white light from the center looking down

00:23:39.430 --> 00:23:42.310
into the silo.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:43.460
There was no wind.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:45.200
There was no noise.

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:49.490
Still only stayed there maybe 20, 30 seconds at most.

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:53.520
And then I just remember--

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:55.680
I'm staring up at the stars, right?

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.000
I'm a pretty keen observer of what's

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.620
above me here in the celestial spear up there

00:24:03.620 --> 00:24:07.750
and I just said to myself what if this thing

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:11.360
beams beams us up and takes us off to some

00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:15.780
distant place and never returned to earth again I mean this is going through

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:17.960
my head here while this thing's above me and

00:24:17.960 --> 00:24:21.900
and then from this dead stop it shoots off to the east

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:26.630
just like now you see it now you don't. It's just phew!

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:30.000
so after this UFO departs

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:36.450
I grabbed my instrument and jumped in the truck behind the steering wheel, and off we went.

00:24:36.550 --> 00:24:38.430
We weren't about to be there if it came back.

00:24:39.130 --> 00:24:42.170
We didn't have guards with us because there was no missile.

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:47.310
We didn't have a radio because we're not really in contact with the Air Force Base.

00:24:47.370 --> 00:24:50.570
I don't know any of this other stuff is even going on, to be honest with you.

00:24:50.570 --> 00:24:57.440
I mean, we're just kind of out there on our own doing these sites and mailing our material back.

00:24:57.660 --> 00:24:58.360
It was...

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:09.420
I wasn't even aware there was a UFO problem per se, but as it turned out, the night's events weren't totally over with us at that point.

00:25:09.500 --> 00:25:21.560
As we sped away and on our way back to Conrad, the Army Corps of Engineers had base-rocked all the roads to take the weight of these missiles they were bringing in.

00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:30.000
And, of course, these are new sites, and they took down all the signs to make the roads wider, and I go over the hill.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.380
and come down. The headlights come down. There's no road there. It teed, you know, and so I

00:25:35.380 --> 00:25:43.270
tried to make a, you either went to the right or left. I tried to go to the left to, towards

00:25:43.270 --> 00:25:50.570
Conrad, and the truck flipped over, and we ended up upside down. Fortunately, none of

00:25:50.570 --> 00:26:00.000
us were hurt. We walked probably about two hours to the nearby farmhouse, if you call

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.300
Montana Highway Patrol.

00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:04.740
The farmer drove us

00:26:04.740 --> 00:26:06.700
back to the accident site

00:26:06.700 --> 00:26:08.420
and it was interesting when the

00:26:08.420 --> 00:26:10.320
highway patrolman arrived

00:26:10.320 --> 00:26:12.470
because we told him, you know,

00:26:12.510 --> 00:26:14.250
how did this occur? He was asking us and

00:26:14.250 --> 00:26:15.070
told him that

00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:18.260
his dispatch had told him there had been over 20

00:26:18.260 --> 00:26:19.760
reports to the

00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.740
to his office

00:26:21.740 --> 00:26:24.320
that night in reporting

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:26.380
a UFO in the area.

00:26:28.980 --> 00:26:30.000
I wrote instant...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.760
incident reports to the

00:26:31.760 --> 00:26:33.740
SATAF, Boeing,

00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:34.980
Montana's

00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:37.640
state

00:26:37.640 --> 00:26:42.040
regarding

00:26:42.040 --> 00:26:43.800
the accident. But, you know,

00:26:43.940 --> 00:26:46.140
what was interesting was I never heard anything

00:26:46.140 --> 00:26:47.520
from the Air Force

00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:49.280
regarding the incident.

00:26:50.110 --> 00:26:51.950
And I never had to

00:26:51.950 --> 00:26:53.210
there was no

00:26:53.210 --> 00:26:56.440
retribution or reimbursement required

00:26:56.440 --> 00:26:58.270
for me for rolling this truck. And this truck

00:26:58.270 --> 00:27:00.000
had 18 miles on it that afternoon.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.490
it was a new truck okay so they nothing they heard nothing so this is this part

00:27:05.490 --> 00:27:12.020
was good because I didn't really want to buy the truck I went back to my

00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:20.170
headquarters at Warren Air Force Base and about a month and a half later I was

00:27:20.170 --> 00:27:25.150
discharged I did not mention wrecking this truck up in Montana on one of my

00:27:25.150 --> 00:27:30.000
TDY's they didn't ask me and I didn't mention it I didn't want to buy it

00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:36.240
But I must say now, my four years that I had with this Geodetic Survey Squadron,

00:27:36.780 --> 00:27:42.310
I had worked on the latest missiles and aircraft in the U.S. Air Force inventory.

00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:49.010
And I worked everywhere on these guidance systems.

00:27:49.490 --> 00:27:56.640
And we, or I never saw anything in the Air Force inventory that could perform like this UFO did.

00:27:56.640 --> 00:28:00.000
I don't know what it was, but...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.930
And we sure didn't have any. I never saw anything like it.

00:28:05.110 --> 00:28:10.130
And I'd like to thank all of you for being here today and thank the National Press Club.

00:28:11.050 --> 00:28:22.660
Hopefully someday we'll know in the near future that the government will perhaps release any information they have on UFOs.

00:28:22.850 --> 00:28:23.670
Thank you very much.

00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:35.570
Hello, everybody. I'm Bruce Fenstermacher.

00:28:35.570 --> 00:28:39.610
I don't have any exciting stories like rolling a truck with 18 miles on it.

00:28:40.840 --> 00:28:47.570
From 1974 to 1976, I was a combat crew commander and a captain in the Air Force

00:28:47.570 --> 00:28:54.230
stationed at F.E. Warren Air Force Base at the 400th SMS and assigned to Romeo flight.

00:28:55.760 --> 00:29:00.000
In the fall of 76, my deputy, who I'll call Sam because he's

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:06.270
not given me permission to release his name we were on alert trying to stay awake we were listening

00:29:06.270 --> 00:29:12.330
to the conversation between the flight security controller of the topside nco and the strategic

00:29:12.330 --> 00:29:19.720
alert team the security alert team the stats kind of that was one way to stay alert because the sac

00:29:19.720 --> 00:29:27.750
duty is moments of terror with hours of boredom and suddenly we heard the fsc call the sat team

00:29:27.750 --> 00:29:29.580
and say, stop the vehicle.

00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:35.530
"Get out of the vehicle and look around." I didn't tell him where to look or anything.

00:29:35.530 --> 00:29:44.060
And Sam and I looked at each other and then said, "What do you see?" And he said, "Oh, I don't see anything. I don't see anything."

00:29:44.060 --> 00:29:55.620
"Holy bleep! I do see a white pulsating light in the sky. It's maybe seven or eight miles away. The FSC asked where it was.

00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:59.730
He said it's to the north. He said it's pretty close to where the

00:30:00.190 --> 00:30:02.900
the launch control facility is.

00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:04.920
So my deputy and I did a double take.

00:30:04.920 --> 00:30:08.530
We called upstairs and we said, "What's going on?"

00:30:08.530 --> 00:30:10.730
He said, "You're not going to believe this, Captain,

00:30:10.730 --> 00:30:14.310
but right above us, there's a huge white thing,

00:30:14.310 --> 00:30:17.710
pulsating light above us."

00:30:17.710 --> 00:30:22.150
And I had to call them to make sure I wasn't seeing anything.

00:30:22.150 --> 00:30:26.590
Upon prodding, he told us it was shaped like a fat cigar.

00:30:26.590 --> 00:30:30.000
I think he said a pregnant cigar, white pulsating light.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:36.460
between the pulsations he saw red and red and blue lights it was silent because

00:30:36.460 --> 00:30:41.560
I prodded him saying is it some for a helicopter he said no it's very silent

00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:46.580
we're talking to him for several minutes and he says it's starting to move away

00:30:46.580 --> 00:30:53.720
along our access road so we hung up my deputy and I saying what do we do we got

00:30:53.720 --> 00:31:00.000
to report this he calls down the FSC calls down shortly and says it's over one hour

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:04.340
launch facilities the missile silos and it was the closest one along the access

00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:11.960
road so I ordered the SAT team to go to that site and they called into through

00:31:11.960 --> 00:31:18.250
the FSE so they had to go back for batteries and they were a little slow

00:31:18.250 --> 00:31:23.830
getting out so I was kind of ordering them come on get get on get going and at

00:31:23.830 --> 00:31:30.000
the same time we contacted the SAC command post and if you aren't and the NCO

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:34.800
answered and we told him the story and he laughed and said when it eats the SAT

00:31:34.800 --> 00:31:44.710
team call me back so the SAT team never got to that LF it silently moved again

00:31:44.710 --> 00:31:49.270
to another launch facility we called the SAT team three or four times I'm sorry

00:31:49.270 --> 00:31:53.750
we called command post three or four times the last time and we got the same

00:31:53.750 --> 00:31:59.150
nonchalant attitude the last time I said are you logging this and they said no

00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:03.050
So I said, give me the officer in charge.

00:32:03.050 --> 00:32:04.070
And he said, well, he's busy.

00:32:04.070 --> 00:32:06.190
I said, well, you either give me the officer in charge

00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:08.930
or I'm going to wake up the base commander, the squadron

00:32:08.930 --> 00:32:10.650
commander, because there's something going on.

00:32:10.650 --> 00:32:12.650
Something's messing with my LFs.

00:32:12.650 --> 00:32:15.130
They were mine for that period.

00:32:15.130 --> 00:32:17.760
So the officer came on.

00:32:17.760 --> 00:32:20.340
I said, you need to log this or I'll wake everybody up.

00:32:20.340 --> 00:32:21.040
He said he would.

00:32:21.040 --> 00:32:24.830
He called his NCO, a different NCO called back

00:32:24.830 --> 00:32:27.510
a few minutes later, took the log of what had happened

00:32:27.510 --> 00:32:30.000
in a timely sequence.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:36.330
it went to another LF. The SAT team had to come back for gas. Then it said it had car

00:32:36.330 --> 00:32:44.290
trouble. It could only go five miles an hour. So long story short, after several, you know,

00:32:44.350 --> 00:32:49.670
about an hour and a half, the flight security controller said he could see it over another

00:32:49.670 --> 00:32:55.380
launch facility down, still down the road. And then he said it suddenly and silently

00:32:55.380 --> 00:32:59.770
just went away up to a star size and then disappeared.

00:33:01.600 --> 00:33:05.680
So that was it. It was exciting rest of the tour. The next day we were relieved by another

00:33:05.680 --> 00:33:12.860
crew to go back home. And I went upstairs and the FSC is lying like in a chair in almost

00:33:12.860 --> 00:33:18.710
a fetal position. And I talked to him and he was scared. He said, I can't sleep. I can't

00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:23.810
get that thing out of my mind. And I said, what the heck was with the SAT team? He said,

00:33:24.040 --> 00:33:30.000
both my deputy and I were prior service. So we got along well with the enlisted guys. So he said, if you promise

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:38.060
not to tell anybody. They told me they were not going to go to any LF with that thing over.

00:33:38.830 --> 00:33:43.960
No direct orders, no nothing. And in fact, they never left the launch control facility.

00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:51.270
We picked up the Quebec team on the way back. The Quebec crew, because Quebec was on the way to

00:33:51.270 --> 00:34:00.000
Romeo. And SAC liked to save a little gas, so we rode share. And they told us that earlier that evening,

00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:08.820
They had the same sort of thing flying over several of their launch facilities.

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:09.820
And I said, "What happened?

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:10.720
You reported it."

00:34:10.720 --> 00:34:13.580
And they said, "Are you crazy?

00:34:13.580 --> 00:34:14.580
We didn't report it.

00:34:14.580 --> 00:34:16.020
We're not going to report it."

00:34:16.020 --> 00:34:17.020
I said, "Well, I did."

00:34:17.020 --> 00:34:22.150
He said, "Well, if you tell them about us, we're going to say it never happened."

00:34:22.150 --> 00:34:23.650
So we went back home.

00:34:23.650 --> 00:34:25.910
I reported to my squadron commander.

00:34:25.910 --> 00:34:30.000
The next few, we always have departure meetings when you go out for alert.

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:37.610
several departure meetings. We had an unusual visitor. We had an officer in a uniform telling us

00:34:37.610 --> 00:34:44.270
that you may have heard rumors about this. It didn't happen. It's top secret. And I wanted to

00:34:44.270 --> 00:34:51.660
stand up and say, which is it? Didn't it happen? Or is it top secret? So that's my event. I think

00:34:51.660 --> 00:34:53.570
Mr. Salas.

00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:05.360
What you have heard here today is evidence of a phenomenon.

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:08.850
It sounds fantastic, and it is fantastic.

00:35:09.750 --> 00:35:13.410
We presented this evidence in the public interest of open government.

00:35:13.530 --> 00:35:19.320
Our signatures on affidavits in the press kit that you have attest to the truth of our statements.

00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:23.200
Our evidence is now public domain.

00:35:23.720 --> 00:35:27.900
The real question is, what is the public going to do with it, this testimony?

00:35:28.080 --> 00:35:30.000
It has been a general practice of the media.

00:35:31.150 --> 00:35:35.050
to scoff at these kinds of stories, make light of such testimony.

00:35:36.080 --> 00:35:39.520
We can only ask that you take the time to give some serious consideration,

00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:47.040
not only to our statements, but to the statements of other witnesses out there who have similar incidents.

00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:52.830
There's also documentary evidence that helps support what we have said.

00:35:53.140 --> 00:35:59.090
We hope you will take the time to at least take a look at those, research this a little bit,

00:36:00.030 --> 00:36:05.430
And if you do, I think you'll come to the same conclusions that we have.

00:36:06.690 --> 00:36:10.580
That is, that the UFO phenomenon is real, not imaginary.

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:16.690
There's current excessive secrecy in our government surrounding this phenomenon.

00:36:18.420 --> 00:36:23.100
Unknown aerial objects have, in fact, been observed over many of our nuclear weapons bases

00:36:23.100 --> 00:36:30.000
and other nuclear facilities, and in some cases, the appearance of these objects coincided with

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:37.890
compromising the operational readiness of our nuclear weapons. Although each of us might have

00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:43.910
different opinions about the meaning and intent of these incidents, I think we can all agree that

00:36:43.910 --> 00:36:48.580
the tampering with nuclear weapons is a national security concern.

00:36:51.300 --> 00:37:00.000
This is Air Force official policy on UFOs. This is dated 2005, but I believe it is

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:07.780
his current policy. I'll just read one part of it. It says no UFO reported, investigated and

00:37:07.780 --> 00:37:15.810
evaluated by the Air Force was ever an indication of threat to our national security. That is

00:37:15.810 --> 00:37:30.000
clearly misleading. It is false based on our testimonies. This statement, the decision to discontinue

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:38.360
The training of UFO investigations was based on an evaluation of a report prepared by the University of Colorado in 1969.

00:37:38.360 --> 00:37:42.260
I believe this was the infamous Condon Committee study.

00:37:44.430 --> 00:37:49.050
There was substantial evidence to show that study was superficial and biased.

00:37:49.570 --> 00:37:55.270
In particular, the Echo and Oscar incidents I spoke about were never investigated by the Condon Committee,

00:37:55.410 --> 00:37:59.290
even though their principal investigator was well aware of these incidents.

00:38:00.480 --> 00:38:05.720
Obviously, the testimony given here today conflicts directly with that Air Force policy

00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:07.130
statement.

00:38:07.130 --> 00:38:12.760
We ask that our government answer to the public about the obvious discrepancy between our

00:38:12.760 --> 00:38:18.120
testimony and that of the current statement.

00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:24.450
Indeed, we demand an answer based on the foundation of our democracy that says, and I want to

00:38:24.450 --> 00:38:28.770
paraphrase Franklin Delano Roosevelt, President Roosevelt.

00:38:30.510 --> 00:38:34.070
The people should be strong enough and well enough informed

00:38:34.070 --> 00:38:39.970
to maintain the sovereign control over its government.

